WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.940
A canal at night.

2
00:00:01.990 --> 00:00:06.060
Black water, a towpath, a single lamp.

3
00:00:06.110 --> 00:00:09.290
One sentence types
itself across the water.

4
00:00:09.340 --> 00:00:11.920
The fog crept along the canal.

5
00:00:11.970 --> 00:00:13.440
Look at that verb again.

6
00:00:13.490 --> 00:00:14.630
Crept.

7
00:00:14.680 --> 00:00:17.700
Creeping takes legs, or at least a body.

8
00:00:17.750 --> 00:00:19.430
Fog has neither.

9
00:00:19.480 --> 00:00:22.640
So why would a writer say the fog crept?

10
00:00:22.690 --> 00:00:26.300
In this mission, you'll meet
metaphor, personification and simile,

11
00:00:26.350 --> 00:00:29.580
and decide which one crept is.

12
00:00:29.630 --> 00:00:33.770
Or is it just accurate, because
fog really does move slowly?

13
00:00:33.820 --> 00:00:37.280
You'll learn a way to read
any image, step by step.

14
00:00:37.330 --> 00:00:42.900
And you'll test it on Dickens, in a city
where "it had not been light all day".

15
00:00:42.950 --> 00:00:47.410
Your mission: explain why the
writer says the fog crept.
